/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  estimatedSpecies01_announced -- WHY THIS CASE EXISTS.

  A species record may mark a formation datum (hfAq, sAq, cpAq) with an origin
  that is not a measurement (estimated, predictive, assumed, placeholder).  The
  engine announces such a datum ONCE per species and datum per run, on the
  [estimate] channel and in the result's provenance, when the run CONSUMES it
  -- here, when the aqueous ion reference of NaOH (sum nu*hfAq, the enthalpy
  datum of the electrolyte) is assembled.  Reading a record is not consuming it.

  No shipped catalogue case consumes an estimated formation datum (the 14
  catalogue species that carry one are organic acid ions no electrolyte case
  reaches yet), so this case MAKES one on purpose: its case-local
  constant/species/OH.dat is the catalogue record with ONE addition, a
  `provenance { hfAq { origin estimated; ... } }` block.  The VALUES are the
  catalogue's, unchanged, so NaOH's activity surface is the one of
  enthalpy_naoh_water; the case is an announcement witness, not a claim that
  the hydroxide enthalpy is estimated (it is a measured NBS value).

  Held by the gate check_estimated_species_announced: it runs this case and
  requires the announcement text and the provenance entry; a run that did not
  consume the datum must say nothing.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
operations
(
    {
        name      gamma_naoh;
        type      electrolyteActivity;
        molality  { from 0.1; to 6.0; n 12; }
        output    { file estimated_witness_naoh.csv; }
    }
);
